ay constraint, forward temporal search from 1006 reaches only 2 nodes and never 1860 (step_01), and no temporal paths are enumerable (step_09). The failure is not caused by the waiting-time bound: with unlimited wait (step_04) and with a relaxed 2400-unit bound (step_15) the target is still unreachable, and even the intermediate hub 743 is unreachable from 1006 (step_14). This means the chain's edges occur in the wrong order (1532's onward contact to 1643 precedes the 1006\u21921532 event), and the chain edges are sparse and non-repeating (step_13: one event per bin, activity ceases after ~37830). Confounders checked: the window has ample overall activity (312 events, 427 active nodes, step_02) and the busiest nodes are unrelated to this pair (step_12), so volume/popularity cannot substitute for the missing temporal ordering. Conclusion: no genuine cascade from 1006 to 1860 in this interval.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 40282, "total_output_tokens": 3022, "total_tokens": 43304, "total_latency_ms": 43508, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}